      <div type="editorial-notes">
        <head>Transcription notes</head>
        <note xml:id="W-3.1-note-1" n="1" type="observation" target="#W-3.1-l1" resp="#W-3.1-encoder">The poem heading and its italic descriptive title are printed immediately before the first verse; the title is retained as source metadata rather than verse text.</note>
        <note xml:id="W-3.1-note-opening-inset" n="2" type="observation" target="#W-3.1-l2" resp="#W-3.1-reviewer">Verse 2 begins beside the two-line initial, approximately three character widths farther right than the ordinary inset verse starts. The additional opening space is based on the actual full-page line starts.</note>
        <note xml:id="W-3.1-note-catch128" n="29" type="uncertainty" target="#W-3.1-catch128" resp="#W-3.1-reviewer">The page-128 catchword begins Im; the heavily inked terminal mark is represented tentatively as a hyphen. Its exact glyph is not secure in this scan.</note>
      </div>
